    {
      "id": 57236,
      "name": "pwatson1974",
      "username": "pwatson1974",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/{size}/1925_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-03-31T14:35:58.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"josephamarino\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/a88e4f/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> josephamarino:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I did a quick search, but I don't think I saw this question answered:Do the three targets for Tempest's Chain Lightning need to be different targets?&nbsp; Can I target a Villain three times with the card, or possibly target Villain-Minion-Villain?We played it as if the targets must be different, because it seemed a little too powerful, otherwise, but I figured I'd ask for the real ruling.&nbsp;Thanks!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Short answer: Yes.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;Long answer: Yeeeeeeeeessssssssss.</p>\n<p>Long answer that isn't a tired joke: Chain lightning refers to a second target and a third target. These can't be the same target because then they'd be the first target rather than the second (or third). This wording also applies to Bunker's Grenade Launcher.</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
